# Frequently Asked Questions

@collapse
@item "What is Markup+?"
Markup+ is a modern markup language that extends Markdown with variables, conditionals, loops, components, charts, math, and RTL support.
@end

@item "Is it free?"
Yes, for non-commercial use. Markup+ is released under the Markup+ Non-Commercial License.
@end

@item "How do I install it?"
```bash
npm install -g markup-plus-js
```
@end

@item "Does it work with Persian?"
Yes — Markup+ detects Persian, Arabic, Hebrew, and Urdu automatically and switches to RTL layout.
@end

@item "Can I use it in production?"
Yes. The package is stable at v0.6.4 with 330 passing tests.
@end
@end
